==Battleground==
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*6 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*9 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Koronium]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 16.67~33.33 seconds<sup>500f~1,000f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 16.67~33.33 seconds<sup>500f~1,000f</sup>.
**18 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
**18 [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A simple stage that introduces [[Koronium]], a Metal [[Kory]] variant with more range and damage than his standard counterpart. However, he has a very small amount of health, allowing any critical hit to dispose of him.

There are a few ways to approach this stage. You can lure Koronium to the base and use a Crit unit like [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] or [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] that outranges them in addition to a Wave Shield like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to protect them from Waves. You can also spam Wave Immune cats and chip down Koronium over time without the need for critical hits.

